flowchart TD
    A[Work on an npm package] --> B{New package<br/>or existing?}

    B -->|New| N1[Scaffold: name, folder,<br/>README H1 all agree]
    B -->|Existing| M0[Audit the metadata]

    N1 --> M0
    M0 --> M1{"repository URL<br/>resolves?"}
    M1 -->|"404 / a docs URL /<br/>missing"| M2[FIX — npmjs.com's Repository<br/>and bugs links are dead]
    M1 -->|Yes| M3
    M2 --> M3{"Another manifest shares<br/>this package name?"}

    M3 -->|Yes| M4[🔴 STOP — resolve to ONE.<br/>Publishing from the wrong dir<br/>ships the wrong tree]
    M3 -->|No| M5[Fill the field contract:<br/>description = README tagline,<br/>funding, keywords, engines,<br/>license, author, homepage, bugs]
    M4 --> M5

    M5 --> F{"files array present?"}
    F -->|"Only .npmignore"| F1[Replace with a files allowlist —<br/>a denylist leaks what it forgot]
    F -->|Yes| F2
    F1 --> F2[Build]

    F2 --> B1[Dual ESM + CJS,<br/>real .d.ts per format,<br/>source maps OFF]
    B1 --> B2[Walk every exports subpath:<br/>types/import/require target<br/>exists on disk]
    B2 --> B3{All resolve?}
    B3 -->|No| B4[Fix the map or the build]
    B4 --> B2
    B3 -->|Yes| D{Dependency review}

    D --> D1{"Does the host app<br/>already own it?"}
    D1 -->|Yes| D2[peerDependency, widest<br/>honest range + a devDep]
    D1 -->|No| D3{"Could ten lines<br/>of our own do it?"}
    D3 -->|Yes| D4[Write the ten lines]
    D3 -->|No| D5[Runtime dependency —<br/>justify it in docs/PACKAGES.md]
    D2 --> DOC
    D4 --> DOC
    D5 --> DOC{Where do the docs live?}

    DOC -->|1| L1[Public docs site]
    DOC -->|2| L2[Public GitHub repo]
    DOC -->|3| L3[Marketing site with real docs]
    DOC -->|4 none exist| L4["Build one:<br/>&lt;npm-name&gt;-docs.aoneahsan.com<br/>GitHub Pages · DNS → MANUAL-TASKS"]

    L1 --> P[Probe the URL:<br/>curl -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}']
    L2 --> P
    L3 --> P
    L4 --> P
    P --> P1{200 or 301?}
    P1 -->|No| P2[Do NOT write it into the README.<br/>Fix the source that named it]
    P2 --> DOC
    P1 -->|Yes| T[Tarball review]

    T --> T1[Ships: dist, README, LICENSE,<br/>CHANGELOG, AI guide]
    T1 --> T2[Never: CLAUDE/AGENTS.md,<br/>internal records, .env, keys]
    T2 --> T3[Verify against the EXTRACTED<br/>tarball, not the repo]
    T3 --> V[Semver + CHANGELOG entry<br/>+ docs/PACKAGES.md]
    V --> G([Hand to the publish gate:<br/>packages-up-to-date])

    style M4 fill:#ffe0e0,stroke:#c00
    style M2 fill:#fff4d6,stroke:#c90
    style P2 fill:#fff4d6,stroke:#c90
    style G fill:#e0f0e0,stroke:#0a0
